{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat collab/exception-track/1795100485885-engineer-dedup-round2-batch2.prompt.md\ncat src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/eval_transport.cljc\nsed -n '1,155p' src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/eval_coordinator.cljc\nsed -n '65,110p' src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/eval_admission.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"Created-GMT: 2026-11-19 15:01:25 GMT\nCreated-Local: 2026-11-19 22:01:25 +07 (Asia/Ho_Chi_Minh)\nCoding-Agent: codex\nSession-ID: pending (provider-generated)\n# Task: yang-dedup-round2-batch2\nRole: Engineer\n\nImplementers:\n- Model: gpt-6.1-terra | Assigned: 2026-11-19 22:01:25 +0700 | Status: active | Rationale: same implementer family as batches/rounds prior; the plan is fully reviewer-fixed (argon audit + conformance amendments, astra dual-role conditions)\n\nImplement round-2 batch 2 in this worktree (detached at current origin/master). You may edit\nfiles and run tests. **Do not commit, do not push, do not touch collab/.** Scratch scripts in\n/tmp. Match surrounding style. Reviewer findings are in the worktree at\ncollab/exception-track/1795020669393-…findings.md (argon audit, sections C4/C5/C6),\n1795022027297-…findings.md (conformance amendments), 1795022967614-…findings.md (astra\nconditions incl. the C5 export-tree signature fix and the eval sanitization preservation) —\nread those sections first.\n\n## Extractions (all reviewer-amended)\n\n### C4: io.clj + io.cljs → src/cljc/yang/io.cljc\n- One cljc file; `#?(:clj … :cljs …)` for the ns header's reader requires and for exactly\n  the two host lines: `read-source` (io/reader vs .readFileSync) and `write-ast` (spit vs\n  .writeFileSync). The other 4 functions (read-forms, compile-file, compile-string,\n  compile-and-save) are character-identical — single bodies. Public API stays 5 entry\n  points. Delete the two old files. Only JVM and Node load yang.io (cljd/jolt do not).\n  Update any ns references if the require path changes (it shouldn't: yang.io stays the name).\n\n### C5: CST internals + export consolidation\n- In `src/clj/yang/antlr/cst.clj`: extract `own-lexer!` and `own-parser!` (private) to match\n  the existing structure of cst.cljs/cst.cljd — removing the duplicated 14-line\n  LexerATNSimulator./ParserATNSimulator. installation blocks in parse-unit and first-failure.\n- Into `src/cljc/yang/antlr/export.cljc`: add `lexer-span` `[offsets start stop]` →\n  `[(offset-at offsets start) (offset-at offsets stop)]` and `export-tree`\n  `[profile unit source errors ops-fn tree]` per the audit — BUT per astra's P2 amendment,\n  the signature must accept the ALREADY-COMPUTED code points and offsets (pass them directly\n  or as one context map), NOT bare `source` (callers compute them before parsing for the\n  error listeners; do not re-compute source-sized offsets on successful parses). Preserve\n  error-first behavior: a syntax-error result must NOT walk the recovered tree. Keep\n  host-specific ops construction in the host files.\n- **Demote in the same pass** (argon conformance amendment): `offset-at`, `export-nodes`,\n  `result` → `defn-` once all four hosts (cst.clj, cst.cljs, cst.cljd, cst.jolt) call the\n  new helpers — export's public surface shrinks 7 → 6 (byte-offsets, token-span,\n  lexer-span, syntax-error, export-tree, failure-kind). Verify zero external callers before\n  each demotion (grep src/ and test/).\n\n### C6: eval rejection-envelope factoring (php-owned surface; the r18 landing released it)\n- Into `src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/eval_transport.cljc` (2 → 4 publics): `correlation`\n  `[request]` → the `[:yang.compile/request :yang.compile/unit :yang.compile/provenance]`\n  select-keys projection (nil-safe: `(when (map? request) …)`), and `rejected`\n  `[request reason extra]` → the rejection map construction (`:yang.compile/outcome\n  :yang.compile/rejected` + reason + merged extra). Replace the 6 repeated constructions in\n  `eval_admission.cljc:77-86` and `eval_coordinator.cljc:61-113` with calls.\n- **Preserve EXACTLY** the special sanitization of invalid transport requests at\n  eval_coordinator.cljc:46 (astra condition) and the r18-added structured-refusal payload\n  with its discriminator `:yang.compile/outcome` inside `:php/fatal` (ruling\n  1795028000000 Q1) — refactor the repetition only, not the payload semantics.\n\n### Hygiene (same pass, argon/amstra list)\n- `yang.antlr.export` demotions (above) and any remaining caller-less publics you can\n  verify: grep before each demotion; if a function has ANY external caller, leave it.\n\n## Mandatory validation plan\n\n1. **Baseline capture BEFORE changes** (script in /tmp): (a) the eval rejection envelopes\n   for the 6 sites' representative inputs — exact maps incl. the r18 discriminator; (b) a\n   CST parse of a fixture with a syntax error AND one clean parse — the error packet + the\n   exported tree + offsets (all four hosts where runnable: JVM clj + Node cljs here;\n   cljd/jolt coverage comes from their lanes, note it); (c) io round-trip: compile-file +\n   write-ast + read back, JVM and Node. Save to /tmp/r2b2-baseline.txt.\n2. **Post-change:** identical outputs (byte/map equality). Any divergence = fix the refactor.\n3. **Focused gates** (report each separately): yang.php.antlr.cst-test (discover exact name\n   via ls test/yang/php/antlr | grep -i cst), the node-targeted CST/io tests if they run via\n   clojure -M:cljs (build with `bb build:yin-repl-node` first; skip if the lane setup is\n   heavy — note it and let the orchestrator run the Node leg), yang.php.antlr eval tests\n   (eval_service_test/eval_bridge_test), yang.python.antlr.parser-test,\n   yang.clojure-test, and yang.php.antlr.include-test quick rows.\n4. `git diff --check` clean.\n\n## Report format (mandatory)\n\nBegin exactly:\nCompleted-GMT: <YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS GMT>\nCompleted-Local: <YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS +07>\n\nThen: per-cluster summary (file:line, before/after, the seam), baseline comparisons\nverbatim, per-invocation test counts, git diff --stat, noticed-but-not-done. End with:\nVERDICT: DONE — <one line> | or | BLOCKED — <why>\n(ns yang.php.antlr.eval-transport\n  \"Validation of the portable, sealed eval compiler request.\")\n\n\n(def request-fields\n  #{:yang.compile/request :yang.compile/unit :yang.compile/frontend-revision\n    :yang.compile/compiler-revision :yang.compile/goal :yang.compile/provenance\n    :yang.compile/options :yang.php/source})\n\n\n(defn portable-data?\n  \"True for the data forms accepted by this request protocol.\"\n  [x]\n  (cond\n    (or (nil? x) (boolean? x) (string? x) (number? x)\n        (keyword? x) (symbol? x)) true\n    (map? x) (every? (fn [[k v]] (and (portable-data? k) (portable-data? v))) x)\n    (or (vector? x) (set? x) (list? x)) (every? portable-data? x)\n    :else false))\n\n\n(defn request-defect\n  \"Return a protocol defect or nil. Unknown fields are refused so that\n   caller runtime state cannot accidentally be included at the top level.\"\n  [request]\n  (cond\n    (not (map? request)) :request-shape\n    (some #(not (contains? request %)) request-fields) :missing-field\n    (some #(not (contains? request-fields %)) (keys request)) :unknown-field\n    (not= :eval (:yang.compile/goal request)) :wrong-goal\n    (not (string? (:yang.php/source request))) :source-shape\n    (not (map? (:yang.compile/options request))) :options-shape\n    (not (portable-data? request)) :non-portable-data\n    :else nil))\n(ns yang.php.antlr.eval-coordinator\n  \"Composition-supplied eval frontend and stream service.\"\n  (:require [dao.jing :as jing]\n            [dao.stream :as stream]\n            [yang.antlr.packet :as packet]\n            [yang.php.antlr.cst :as cst]\n            [yang.php.antlr.eval-admission :as admission]\n            [yang.php.antlr.eval-publication :as publication]\n            [yang.php.antlr.eval-transport :as transport]\n            [yang.php.antlr.scope :as scope]\n            [yang.php.antlr.siteset :as siteset]))\n\n\n(defn make-worker\n  []\n  (cst/make-eval-worker))\n\n\n(defn compile-request\n  \"Prepare one request for later eval-unit emission. Identity includes the\n   complete request (including bytes and caller-supplied revisions/options),\n   the source goal, grammar and admission profile. No caller runtime state is\n   needed by this service.\"\n  [worker request]\n  (let [{:keys [source] :as admitted} (admission/admit-request request)]\n    (if-not source\n      admitted\n      (let [pk (cst/parse-source worker (:yang.compile/unit request) source)\n            identity {:request request\n                      :yang.php/source (:yang.php/source request)\n                      :yang.php.eval/profile-revision admission/profile-revision\n                      :yang.php/source-goal :eval\n                      :yang.php/grammar cst/grammar-id}]\n        (if (:yang.php/not-php pk)\n          {:request request :identity identity :cst pk}\n          (let [validated (packet/validate! pk {:source source})]\n            (cond-> {:request request :identity identity :cst validated}\n              (= :yang.cst/ok (:yang.cst/outcome validated))\n              (assoc :scope (scope/analyze validated)))))))))\n\n\n(defn compile-transport-request\n  \"Validate a sealed transport request before handing it to the parser worker.\n   Refusals include the request identity only when it is portable data.\"\n  [worker request]\n  (if-let [defect (transport/request-defect request)]\n    (cond-> {:yang.compile/outcome :yang.compile/rejected\n             :yang.compile/reason :yang.compile/invalid-request\n             :yang.compile/detail defect}\n      (and (map? request) (contains? request :yang.compile/request)\n           (transport/portable-data? (:yang.compile/request request)))\n      (assoc :yang.compile/request (:yang.compile/request request)))\n    (compile-request worker request)))\n\n\n(defn- compile-and-publish*!\n  \"Compile a sealed request and publish its canonical module and occurrence\n   set to the composition's store. Linker admission is a separate step.\"\n  [{:keys [worker store registry stage-requirement]} request]\n  (let [{:keys [cst identity] :as prepared} (compile-transport-request worker request)\n        correlation (when (map? request)\n                      (select-keys request [:yang.compile/request :yang.compile/unit\n                                            :yang.compile/provenance]))]\n    (cond\n      (:yang.compile/outcome prepared) prepared\n      (not= :yang.cst/ok (:yang.cst/outcome cst))\n      (merge correlation {:yang.compile/outcome :yang.compile/rejected\n                          :yang.compile/reason :yang.compile/invalid-source\n                          :yang.compile/diagnostics (:yang.cst/errors cst)})\n      :else\n      (let [name (symbol (str \"eval.\" (name (jing/segment-key identity))))\n            result (publication/publish! store registry name prepared)]\n        (if (= :ok (:status result))\n          (let [address (:address result)\n                site (:sites result)\n                stage (when stage-requirement\n                        (siteset/stage registry stage-requirement\n                                       {address [(:record-address site)]}))\n                derived (when stage (stage {:store store :datoms [] :principals []}\n                                           name address))]\n            (if (and derived (not= :ok (:status derived)))\n              (merge correlation {:yang.compile/outcome :yang.compile/rejected\n                                  :yang.compile/reason :yang.compile/derivation-failed\n                                  :yang.compile/detail derived})\n              (merge correlation {:yang.compile/outcome :yang.compile/published\n                                  :yang.compile/module name\n                                  :yang.compile/address address\n                                  :yang.compile/source-address (:source-address result)\n                                  :yang.compile/site-record (:record-address site)}\n                     (when derived {:yang.compile/active-address (:address derived)\n                                    :yang.compile/derivation (:derivation derived)}))))\n          (merge correlation {:yang.compile/outcome :yang.compile/rejected\n                              :yang.compile/reason :yang.compile/publication-failed\n                              :yang.compile/detail (select-keys result [:reason :status])}))))))\n\n\n(defn compile-and-publish!\n  \"Compile and publish, returning classified frontend diagnostics to the caller.\"\n  [state request]\n  (try\n    (compile-and-publish*! state request)\n    (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Exception :cljs :default) e\n      (let [diagnostic (ex-data e)]\n        (if (:yang.php/diagnostic diagnostic)\n          (merge (when (map? request)\n                   (select-keys request [:yang.compile/request :yang.compile/unit\n                                         :yang.compile/provenance]))\n                 {:yang.compile/outcome :yang.compile/rejected\n                  :yang.compile/reason (if (= :yang.php/compile-error\n                                              (:yang.php/diagnostic diagnostic))\n                                         :yang.compile/invalid-source\n                                         :yang.compile/unsupported)\n                  :yang.compile/diagnostic diagnostic})\n          (throw e))))))\n\n\n(defn serve\n  \"Serve at most `budget` requests. Advance the immutable request cursor only\n   after its answer is appended, so a full response stream loses no request.\"\n  ([state] (serve state 32))\n  ([state budget]\n   (loop [state state, remaining budget]\n     (if (not (pos? remaining))\n       state\n       (let [read (or (:pending state)\n                      (let [item (stream/next (:requests state) (:cursor state))]\n                        (when (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome item))\n                          {:cursor (:dao.stream/cursor item)\n                           :answer (compile-and-publish! state (:dao.stream/value item))})))]\n         (if read\n           (let [written (stream/append! (:responses state) (:answer read))]\n             (if (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome written))\n               (recur (-> state (assoc :cursor (:cursor read)) (dissoc :pending))\n                      (dec remaining))\n               (assoc state :pending read)))\n           state))))))\n                encoded (mapv #(bit-and % 255) (text/utf8-encode source))]\n            (if (= bs encoded)\n              {:source source}\n              (throw (ex-info \"UTF-8 round trip failed\" {:reason :utf8-round-trip})))))))))\n\n\n(defn admit-request\n  \"Admit a sealed eval request, preserving correlation and provenance on refusal.\n   On success the original request and its derived parser view travel together.\"\n  [request]\n  (let [{:keys [source diagnostic reason]} (admit (:yang.php/source request))]\n    (cond\n      diagnostic (assoc (select-keys request [:yang.compile/request :yang.compile/unit\n                                              :yang.compile/provenance])\n                        :yang.compile/outcome :yang.compile/rejected\n                        :yang.compile/reason :yang.compile/unsupported\n                        :yang.compile/diagnostic diagnostic)\n      reason (assoc (select-keys request [:yang.compile/request :yang.compile/unit\n                                          :yang.compile/provenance])\n                    :yang.compile/outcome :yang.compile/rejected\n                    :yang.compile/reason :yang.compile/invalid-request\n                    :yang.compile/detail reason)\n      :else {:request request :source source})))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
