arser) cps offsets tree))))\nsrc/cljs/yang/io.cljs:1:(ns yang.io\nsrc/clj/yang/io.clj:1:(ns yang.io\ntest/yang/clojure_test.clj:8:            [yang.io :as yang-io]\ntest/yang/clojure_test.clj:56:  (let [ast (first (yang-io/compile-string \"(+ x\\n   (* x 2))\"))]\n15:P2 | [Round-2 audit:333](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/exception-track/1795020669393-architect-yang-dedup-round2-audit.gemini-4-argon-high.findings.md:333); [cst.clj:127](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/clj/yang/antlr/cst.clj:127) | C5 proposes `export-tree [profile unit source errors ops-fn tree]`. Callers already compute code points and offsets before parsing because error listeners need them. Jolt also needs offsets to convert diagnostic records. Passing only `source` requires the exporter to repeat this source-sized computation and allocation on successful parses. | Pass the already-computed code points and offsets, directly or in one context map. Preserve the existing error-first behavior: a syntax-error result must not walk the recovered tree. Keep host-specific `ops` construction in the host files.\n21:P2 | [Review prompt:79](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/exception-track/1795022967614-astra-dedup-round2-dual-role-review.prompt.md:79); [conformance.clj:23](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yang/call/conformance.clj:23); [siteset_test.cljc:86](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yang/python/antlr/siteset_test.cljc:86) | The four backends do not exercise identical admission paths. The linked conformance harness explicitly covers semantic/register/stack and excludes the AST walker; separate prelude parity tests cover all four. Also, existing site-address tests compare two publications produced by the same implementation, so a deterministic address change could pass. The amended plan supplies no explicit validation gate resolving these distinctions. | Require separate four-backend prelude parity and three-backend linked-module checks, plus before/after fixtures for canonical rows, site-set bytes, record bytes and addresses. Compare refusal messages and `ex-data` exactly. This is a validation-plan gap, not an observed runtime regression.\n51:- The eight consumer edges are gross additions. Including four removed edges and the new namespace’s two foundational edges, C2 plus the split adds **six net edges**. C6 separately adds one `eval-admission → eval-transport` edge.\n84:Move every sentinel comparison with the reader: the auto-qualified `::absent` keyword changes namespace. This is a local sentinel change, not a wire-format change. Loading also remains distinct from subsequent row validation.\n101:Thus the source comparison supports semantic preservation, subject to the distinct validation paths identified above. It does not establish new linked-AST support or prove arbitrary cross-backend continuation migration.\n115:3. Run four-backend prelude parity separately from linked semantic/register/stack checks.\n116:4. For Batch 2, verify all four CST hosts, including Unicode spans, synthetic tokens and syntax-error packets; verify JVM/Node I/O branches and PHP rejection-envelope equality. Preserve the special sanitization of invalid transport requests at [eval_coordinator.cljc:46](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/eval_coordinator.cljc:46).\n120:DUAL-ROLE VERDICT: DISPATCH WITH AMENDMENTS — Reuse prepared source offsets in C5 and add explicit address-preservation and separate AST/linked-VM validation gates.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
